    description: "Found by the 2026-11-24 docstring staleness audit (dev 7e204b35b): a reviewer flagged it and a default-REJECT verifier re-reproduced it on a fixture of its own (reports under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/staleness_audit_11242026/review and verify). Corpus impact not measured. _extract_inheritance_edges (ruby.py:3879-3891) checks the lexical nesting then the top level, never the ancestors (include M) of the enclosing scope. `module A; include M; class Q < Base` extends a top-level Base, while `Base.new.hi` in the same module resolves to M::Base#hi. The module docstring (L78-84) and commit 8fc6a3fcb name a superclass among the constants resolved through ancestors. r15, v05."  # cb9e
